{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE — the code-verifiable criteria are met; ONE criterion legitimately awaits a live harness run.\n\nMERGED as Gerrit change 1118, in origin/main at 09be45933 (content confirmed:\n`git show origin/main:tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py` resolves).\n\nTHE REPRODUCTION, BEFORE AND AFTER. A client serving 250 issues while capping every page at 20 (a\nlowered `jira.search.views.default.max`, the documented DC hardening):\n\n    before: 20 of 250 recovered  — 92% of the inbound snapshot silently lost\n    after : 250 of 250 recovered\n\nRun against `fetcher.collect(..., page_size=100)` directly, not inferred from the diff.\n\nPER-CRITERION\n * \"the 250/20 reproduction recovers 250, asserted by a held-out unit test that FAILS on the current\n   code\" — MET. `test_a_server_capped_page_does_not_end_the_scan`; confirmed RED before the fix\n   (recovered 20) and green after.\n * \"termination is on an EMPTY page only, and the advance is by `len(page)`\" — MET, readable at\n   `fetcher.py`'s pager: `start_at += len(page)`, with the early `if not page: return` as the sole\n   terminator.\n * \"a `startAt`-ignoring server raises `SilentTruncationError` instead of looping, with a bounded-time\n   guarantee\" — MET, `test_a_server_that_ignores_start_at_on_a_full_page_raises_rather_than_looping`\n   (bounded at 100 calls so a hang fails the test rather than the suite).\n * \"the existing `cap`, ACLI-ceiling and `same-token-twice` behaviours are unchanged, each asserted by\n   a test that exercises them\" — MET, four tests. This mattered: `cap` was ALSO broken by the original\n   defect (`cap=45` yielded 20, because truncation ended the scan before the cap was reached), which\n   the cap test caught and which I had not predicted.\n * \"the full unit suite passes\" — MET locally: 1720 passed in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler, plus lint\n   and mypy clean. NOTE the caveat now recorded in the handoff: local pytest is NOT a faithful CI\n   oracle on this machine (CI runs py3.11; this host has only 3.13/3.14). The authoritative signal is\n   the Verified +1 this change received before submit.\n * \"the live DC harness job stays green\" — **NOT YET MET, and correctly so.** No harness run has\n   executed against a main containing this change. A run is queued behind changes 1124 and 1127; I\n   will record the run id and the JOB result (not the overall run status) here before re-closing.\n\nTWO DESIGN CORRECTIONS MADE DURING IMPLEMENTATION, recorded because both were caught by tests rather\nthan by review:\n 1. The first offset-stall guard raised on ANY repeated page, which broke seven existing tests whose\n    doubles ignore `startAt` entirely. Narrowed to: a repeated FULL page raises (the server claims\n    more while never advancing, so the loop would never terminate), a repeated SHORT page stops\n    cleanly (an offset-blind client with nothing left to give). This does not weaken the fix — a\n    hardened DC honours `startAt`, so its second capped page holds DIFFERENT issues and the scan\n    continues.\n 2. The stall check initially ran AFTER the yield, so the duplicate page reached the caller and drove\n    duplicate creates in a dry-run pass that must write nothing. Moved before the yield. Caught only\n    because two orchestration tests assert \"writes nothing\"."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785523133942058001,"uuid":"fd9ea32c-54dd-4d3e-a310-4412ca86b49d"}